From 1bfdb73ee6331a0a98214e2abd81c24e2d4b13f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dongming Han <handongming@gl-inet.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 12:23:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dnsproxy: trim unused encrypted downstream listeners

Split encrypted downstream listener setup into build-tagged files.  The
trimmed build keeps plain UDP/TCP downstream DNS while compiling out unused TLS,
HTTPS, QUIC, and DNSCrypt downstream listeners.

This only affects downstream listener code.  Upstream protocol support remains
available for both full and trimmed downstream builds.
